Title: FINAL LAP
Author: Tyler Brooks
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. UNIVERSITY POOL - MORNING

Lane lines cut still water. COACH ALMA REYES, 50s, watches NINA VASQUEZ, 22, sprint intervals — fast, angry, precise.
ALMA
Elbows higher on the turn. You're racing the clock, not your ghost.

INT. ATHLETIC TRAINING ROOM - DAY

Nina ices her shoulder. A TV replays last year's nationals — Nina finishing fourth, touching the wall a breath too late.
NINA
One hundredth of a second. That's not a ghost. That's math.

INT. COACH'S OFFICE - DAY

Alma slides a meet invitation across the desk — SENIOR INVITATIONAL, Nina's last eligible meet.
ALMA
You swim or you retire wondering. No middle lane.

INT. UNIVERSITY POOL - NIGHT

Empty stands. Nina dives alone — brutal pace. Her stroke falters at 150 meters. She slams the lane rope, gasping.
NINA
I can't hit the split. Not clean. Not ever.

INT. UNIVERSITY POOL - DAY

Meet day. Blocks set. Alma touches Nina's cap — wordless. Nina settles into stillness. The starter raises his pistol.
NINA
(to herself)
Not fourth. Not almost.

FADE OUT.


THE END
